From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 13:05:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ec/lenovo/h8: Add \BLTH and \WGSV for thinkpad_acpi

At shutdown thinkpad_acpi asks the firmware to save the state of the
Bluetooth and WWAN radios for S4/S5, with \BLTH(5) and \WGSV(4) of the
OEM firmware. Without them it prints two errors on the console of every
shutdown and reboot:

  thinkpad_acpi: acpi_evalf(\BLTH, vd, ...) failed: AE_NOT_FOUND
  thinkpad_acpi: acpi_evalf(\WGSV, vd, ...) failed: AE_NOT_FOUND

HKEY already keeps the state at resume (SBDC and SWAN, bit 2), so there
is nothing to save: add both methods, with the other commands of the OEM
firmware reading and setting that same state.

TEST=ThinkPad W541: the DSDT compiles with the methods at the root scope.

Co-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 src/ec/lenovo/h8/acpi/thinkpad.asl | 46 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 46 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/ec/lenovo/h8/acpi/thinkpad.asl b/src/ec/lenovo/h8/acpi/thinkpad.asl
index 28877a61..497666c6 100644
--- a/src/ec/lenovo/h8/acpi/thinkpad.asl
+++ b/src/ec/lenovo/h8/acpi/thinkpad.asl
@@ -333,3 +333,49 @@ Device (HKEY)
 	#include "thinkpad_bat_thresholds.asl"
 	#endif
 }
+
+/*
+ * \BLTH and \WGSV of the OEM firmware: thinkpad_acpi calls them at shutdown
+ * (\BLTH 5 and \WGSV 4, "save the radio state for S4/S5") and prints an
+ * AE_NOT_FOUND error on the console without them. The state at resume is
+ * already kept in HKEY (SBDC and SWAN, bit 2); the other commands read or
+ * set that same state.
+ */
+Scope (\)
+{
+	/*
+	 * Arg0: 0 get Ultraport ID, 1 get state at resume, 2 on at resume,
+	 * 3 off at resume, 5 save the state
+	 */
+	Method (BLTH, 1)
+	{
+		If (Arg0 == 1) {
+			Return (\_SB.PCI0.LPCB.EC.HKEY.WBDC)
+		}
+		If (Arg0 == 2) {
+			\_SB.PCI0.LPCB.EC.HKEY.WBDC = 1
+		}
+		If (Arg0 == 3) {
+			\_SB.PCI0.LPCB.EC.HKEY.WBDC = 0
+		}
+		Return (0)
+	}
+
+	/*
+	 * Arg0: 1 get the state (the bits of GWAN), 2 on at resume, 3 off at
+	 * resume, 4 save the state
+	 */
+	Method (WGSV, 1)
+	{
+		If (Arg0 == 1) {
+			Return (\_SB.PCI0.LPCB.EC.HKEY.GWAN ())
+		}
+		If (Arg0 == 2) {
+			\_SB.PCI0.LPCB.EC.HKEY.WWAN = 1
+		}
+		If (Arg0 == 3) {
+			\_SB.PCI0.LPCB.EC.HKEY.WWAN = 0
+		}
+		Return (0)
+	}
+}
